  <LuaFunction Name="_JBTFE_PRX_name()" ReturnType="String" Description="Returns a CAD system block name to represent a specific proxy object variant.">
   <Signature>String _JBTFE_PRX_name()</Signature>
   <Formula>
				function _JBTFE_PRX_name()
					local usage = [[
Property 'name'
===============================
2025-10-12_000 CLFEY Created.

This is your how-to guide to assign suitable names to all your proxy object variants.

For each proxy variant, the Lua formula below shall return the content of the 'name' property for instances of a specific proxy
variant. You may also choose to delete this Lua formula and just state a simple text value in each concrete proxy object.

Press F3 to open the Lua editor, then hover over the Lua function name and press F5 to copy the Lua formula from DNA to the current object.
]]

					local myProxyObjectName
					
					--Replace 'Variant' in the Lua code below with a suitable name for each proxy variant that you need. Example: "Telephone "..Seq
						if Variant == "Proxy variant 1"  then myProxyObjectName = Variant
					elseif Variant == "Proxy variant 2"  then myProxyObjectName = Variant
					elseif Variant == "Proxy variant 3"  then myProxyObjectName = Variant
					elseif Variant == "Proxy variant 4"  then myProxyObjectName = Variant
					elseif Variant == "Proxy variant 5"  then myProxyObjectName = Variant
					elseif Variant == "Proxy variant 6"  then myProxyObjectName = Variant
					elseif Variant == "Proxy variant 7"  then myProxyObjectName = Variant
					elseif Variant == "Proxy variant 8"  then myProxyObjectName = Variant
					elseif Variant == "Proxy variant 9"  then myProxyObjectName = Variant
					elseif Variant == "Proxy variant 10" then myProxyObjectName = Variant
					elseif Variant == "Proxy variant 11" then myProxyObjectName = Variant
					elseif Variant == "Proxy variant 12" then myProxyObjectName = Variant
					elseif Variant == "Proxy variant 13" then myProxyObjectName = Variant
					elseif Variant == "Proxy variant 14" then myProxyObjectName = Variant
					elseif Variant == "Proxy variant 15" then myProxyObjectName = Variant
					elseif Variant == "Proxy variant 16" then myProxyObjectName = Variant
					elseif Variant == "Proxy variant 17" then myProxyObjectName = Variant
					elseif Variant == "Proxy variant 18" then myProxyObjectName = Variant
					elseif Variant == "Proxy variant 19" then myProxyObjectName = Variant
					elseif Variant == "Proxy variant 20" then myProxyObjectName = Variant
					else return "Unrecognized proxy variant ["..Variant.."]." --(should not be possible...)
					end
					
					return myProxyObjectName, _info(usage)
				end
			</Formula>
  </LuaFunction>
  <CustomProperty DataType="String" Name="ProxySymbolBlockName" DisplayName="Proxy symbol blockname" Description="The name of a Block Table entry (a 2D symbol) created using the CAD editor's block editor command (BEDIT or just BE). Graphic entities inside your block (polylines etc) must reside on layer 0 with color 'ByBlock' if you want the graphics to be displayed in the color of the proxy object's layer. If your 2D symbol needs a text inside it, then add an attribute definition entity (write 'ATTDEF' in the Block Editor) and name its tag 'PROXYTEXT'. If you want your 2D symbol (and its ATTDEF text if it has one) to scale along with your drawing's scale, then bring up the CAD system's property manager (Ctrl+1) inside the block editor (with nothing selected) and check the 'Annotative' option for the block itself." DefaultValue="NO-BN-2D-JBTRC_THUMBNAIL-USPESIFISERT-{{SymbolMode}}" Category="General"/>
  <LuaExpression Name="ProxySymbolBlockName">
   <Formula>_JBTFE_PRX_ProxySymbolBlockName()</Formula>
  </LuaExpression>
  <LuaFunction Name="_JBTFE_PRX_ProxySymbolBlockName()" ReturnType="String" Description="Returns a CAD system block name to represent a specific proxy object variant.">
   <Signature>String _JBTFE_PRX_ProxySymbolBlockName()</Signature>
   <Formula>
				function _JBTFE_PRX_ProxySymbolBlockName()
					local usage = [[
Property 'ProxySymbolBlockName'
===============================
2025-10-12_000 CLFEY Created.

This is your how-to guide to assign the right graphics to each of your own proxy variants.

For each proxy variant that you want to define, this Lua formula shall return the name of a CAD system block of your choice. You may
also choose to delete this Lua formula and just state the correct CAD system block name as a simple text value.

Press F3 to open the Lua editor, then hover over the Lua function name and press F5 to copy the Lua formula from DNA to the current object.


Note on annotative graphics
---------------------------
The default proxy symbol's block name comes in two flavors, 'Schematic' and 'Geographic'. The RailCOMPLETE standard library contains this
proxy symbol both as fixed-size and fairly large graphics with the block name 'NO-BN-2D-JBTRC_THUMBNAIL-USPESIFISERT-Schematic', but also 
as an annotative (scalable graphics) version with the block name 'NO-BN-2D-JBTRC_THUMBNAIL-USPESIFISERT-Geographic'. If you want your 
graphics in both of these flavors, then we advise you to store your schematic block for proxy type 'n' as 'YOUR-BLOCK-NAME-n-Schematic'
and 'YOUR-BLOCK-NAME-n-Geographic'. The reason is that you may, after inserting these proxy variants, switch the 'SymbolMode' property,
found in the Property Manager under the '2D Presentation' tab, between 'Schematic' and 'Geographic'. RailCOMPLETE will interpret your Lua 
code when it sees {{SymbolMode}} inside double curly braces and translate this into the current value of the property 'SymbolMode'. The 
'SymbolMode' property holds either 'Schematic' = fixed-size graphics or 'Geographic' = annotative = graphics that changes size as you 
change the drawing's scale.
]]
					
					local defaultBlockName = "NO-BN-2D-JBTRC_THUMBNAIL-USPESIFISERT-{{SymbolMode}}"
					local blockName
					
					--Replace 'defaultBlockName' with your own block name for each proxy variant that you need:
						if Variant == "Proxy variant 1"  then blockName = defaultBlockName
					elseif Variant == "Proxy variant 2"  then blockName = defaultBlockName
					elseif Variant == "Proxy variant 3"  then blockName = defaultBlockName
					elseif Variant == "Proxy variant 4"  then blockName = defaultBlockName
					elseif Variant == "Proxy variant 5"  then blockName = defaultBlockName
					elseif Variant == "Proxy variant 6"  then blockName = defaultBlockName
					elseif Variant == "Proxy variant 7"  then blockName = defaultBlockName
					elseif Variant == "Proxy variant 8"  then blockName = defaultBlockName
					elseif Variant == "Proxy variant 9"  then blockName = defaultBlockName
					elseif Variant == "Proxy variant 10" then blockName = defaultBlockName
					elseif Variant == "Proxy variant 11" then blockName = defaultBlockName
					elseif Variant == "Proxy variant 12" then blockName = defaultBlockName
					elseif Variant == "Proxy variant 13" then blockName = defaultBlockName
					elseif Variant == "Proxy variant 14" then blockName = defaultBlockName
					elseif Variant == "Proxy variant 15" then blockName = defaultBlockName
					elseif Variant == "Proxy variant 16" then blockName = defaultBlockName
					elseif Variant == "Proxy variant 17" then blockName = defaultBlockName
					elseif Variant == "Proxy variant 18" then blockName = defaultBlockName
					elseif Variant == "Proxy variant 19" then blockName = defaultBlockName
					elseif Variant == "Proxy variant 20" then blockName = defaultBlockName
					else return "Unrecognized proxy variant ["..Variant.."]." --(should not be possible...)
					end
					
					return blockName, _info(usage)
				end
			</Formula>
  </LuaFunction>
  <CustomProperty DataType="String" Name="ProxySymbolAttDefText" DisplayName="Proxy symbol's text inside its 2D symbol" Description="The text to be inserted inside the proxy symbol, provided that it contains a CAD system attribute definition entity (ATTDEF) using the tag ame 'PROXYTEXT'. See also the explanation to property 'ProxySymbolBlockname'." DefaultValue="(insert the text intended for ATTDEF 'PROXYTEXT' in your proxy symbol)" Category="General"/>
  <LuaExpression Name="ProxySymbolAttDefText">
   <Formula>_JBTFE_PRX_ProxySymbolAttDefText()</Formula>
  </LuaExpression>
  <LuaFunction Name="_JBTFE_PRX_ProxySymbolAttDefText()" ReturnType="String" Description="Returns a CAD system block name to represent a specific proxy object variant.">
   <Signature>String _JBTFE_PRX_ProxySymbolAttDefText()</Signature>
   <Formula>
				function _JBTFE_PRX_ProxySymbolAttDefText()
					local usage = [[
Property 'ProxySymbolAttDefText'
===============================
2025-10-12_000 CLFEY Created.

This is your how-to guide to feed an ATTDEF entity with Tag = 'PROXYTEXT' found inside your own proxy object blocks with suitable text values of your choice.
Note: RailCOMPLETE will ignore an ATTDEF in your proxy symbol block if its Tag is not 'PROXYTEXT'.

For each proxy variant that you want to treat, this Lua formula shall return the text to be shown inside the proxy object's 2D symbol, as represented by
the 'PROXYTEXT' ATTDEF in that CAD block definition.

Press F3 to open the Lua editor, then hover over the Lua function name and press F5 to copy the Lua formula from DNA to the current object.

After you have modified the formula, spread it to all your Proxy objects using the RC-EditProperty command, selecting the 
'ProxySymbolAttDefText' property and then using the 'Pick' option to select a Lua formula to apply to all proxy objects. There is
no way a regular user can modify the default value of the next proxy object that you create using RC-InsertPointObject, you must
instead copy an existing, or insert a new one from DNA and modify its formulas afterwards.]]
					
					local defaultProxySymbolText = "MyProxyText"
					local proxySymbolText
					
					--Replace 'defaultProxySymbolText' with your own proxy symbol text for each proxy variant that you need.
					if Variant == "Proxy type 1" then proxySymbolText = defaultProxySymbolText
					elseif Variant == "Proxy variant 2" then proxySymbolText = defaultProxySymbolText
					elseif Variant == "Proxy variant 3" then proxySymbolText = defaultProxySymbolText
					elseif Variant == "Proxy variant 4" then proxySymbolText = defaultProxySymbolText
					elseif Variant == "Proxy variant 5" then proxySymbolText = defaultProxySymbolText
					elseif Variant == "Proxy variant 6" then proxySymbolText = defaultProxySymbolText
					elseif Variant == "Proxy variant 7" then proxySymbolText = defaultProxySymbolText
					elseif Variant == "Proxy variant 8" then proxySymbolText = defaultProxySymbolText
					elseif Variant == "Proxy variant 9" then proxySymbolText = defaultProxySymbolText
					elseif Variant == "Proxy variant 10" then proxySymbolText = defaultProxySymbolText
					elseif Variant == "Proxy variant 11" then proxySymbolText = defaultProxySymbolText
					elseif Variant == "Proxy variant 12" then proxySymbolText = defaultProxySymbolText
					elseif Variant == "Proxy variant 13" then proxySymbolText = defaultProxySymbolText
					elseif Variant == "Proxy variant 14" then proxySymbolText = defaultProxySymbolText
					elseif Variant == "Proxy variant 15" then proxySymbolText = defaultProxySymbolText
					elseif Variant == "Proxy variant 16" then proxySymbolText = defaultProxySymbolText
					elseif Variant == "Proxy variant 17" then proxySymbolText = defaultProxySymbolText
					elseif Variant == "Proxy variant 18" then proxySymbolText = defaultProxySymbolText
					elseif Variant == "Proxy variant 19" then proxySymbolText = defaultProxySymbolText
					elseif Variant == "Proxy variant 20" then proxySymbolText = defaultProxySymbolText
					else return "Unrecognized Variant ["..Variant.."]."
					end
					
					return proxySymbolText, _info(usage)
				end
			</Formula>
  </LuaFunction>
